---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
---

<Page
  title="Waymark pricing: one price, no subscription"
  description="Start free with chapters 1 and 2 and a mock exam. Unlock everything for £9.99, paid once. No subscription, no auto-renewal, no adverts."
  heading="One price. No subscription."
  lead="Start free. If Waymark helps, unlock everything with a single payment. Nothing renews and there are no adverts."
>
  <div class="price-grid">
    <div class="price-card">
      <h3>Free</h3>
      <p class="price">£0</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Chapters 1 and 2 in full</li>
        <li>Quick 24-question check</li>
        <li>One timed mock exam</li>
        <li>Free practice test and chapter samples on this site</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="btn secondary" href="/app">Start free</a>
    </div>
    <div class="price-card featured">
      <h3>Standard</h3>
      <p class="price">£9.99 <small>one-off</small></p>
      <ul>
        <li>All five chapters and every question</li>
        <li>Unlimited mock exams</li>
        <li>Daily plan and spaced review to your test date</li>
        <li>Works offline, no adverts</li>
        <li>Use it on up to 3 of your own devices</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="btn" href="/app/unlock">Buy Standard · £9.99</a>
    </div>
    <div class="price-card">
      <h3>Plus</h3>
      <p class="price">£14.99 <small>one-off</small></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Everything in Standard</li>
        <li>Explanations in your language</li>
        <li>"Explain my mistake" tutor</li>
      </ul>
      <p><em>Coming soon.</em></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="note">Payments open at launch. Until then, everything in the app is free to try in preview.</p>

  <h2>What "one-off" means</h2>
  <p>
    You pay once and keep access for the current edition of the official handbook (3rd edition). There is no
    subscription and nothing renews. If the Home Office publishes a new handbook within 12 months of your purchase, you
    get the new-edition content at no extra cost.
  </p>

  <h2>Pass promise</h2>
  <p>
    We plan to offer a money-back promise: if you follow the plan, reach the readiness standard and still don't pass,
    we refund what you paid. The full terms will be published on our <a href="/pass-promise">pass promise page</a>
    before it applies to any purchase.
  </p>

  <h2>For libraries, advisers and colleges</h2>
  <p>Voucher packs and site licences are available. See <a href="/for-organisations">Waymark for organisations</a>.</p>
</Page>
